# Engine files that include a shell header.
#
# ONE, and it is not debt. types.h -> tune.h is deliberate: the include sits
# after types.h's own #endif so the SPSA macros reach anywhere types.h does, and
# removing it would make every future tuning run add an include first.
#
# Nothing else belongs here. The engine does not print; it emits through the
# output-sink seam, so an engine file including a console or UCI header is a new
# violation to close rather than an entry to add.
types.h -> tune.h
